              "isFalsePositive": false,
              "reasoning": "The entire source\u2192sink path is visible: `request.form['expression']` (line 116, attacker-controlled) is passed to `eval()` and the result is concatenated directly into the raw HTML response string (line 120) with no HTML encoding/escaping. The only transformation is `.replace('\\n', '\\n<br>')` which is not an XSS mitigation. An attacker can submit an expression like `'<script>alert(1)</script>'` which evaluates to that string and is reflected unescaped into the response. (The `eval()` also constitutes arbitrary code execution, making this even more severe than the XSS label suggests.)",
              "promptHash": "50dd7c1cafbcd40d09eb2d1a96caacb932d736acc1e0bcc55a28236e97c0a4e7",
