            "polygraph": {
              "verdict": "TRUE_POSITIVE",
              "isFalsePositive": false,
              "reasoning": "I read the entire app.py (all 211 lines): the /evaluate route (lines 111\u2013130) has no auth decorator and no session check in its body, and there is no @app.before_request hook, login_manager, or any other global auth mechanism anywhere in the file. A repo-wide search for before_request/login_required/login_manager found no matches in this project (all hits are in other realvuln-* apps), and the project directory contains only app.py as application code, so no external module can supply a global auth hook. The only auth check in the app is the per-route session.get('logged_in') in home() (line 35), which does not apply to /evaluate \u2014 an unauthenticated user can freely reach the endpoint (which also eval()s user input at line 120) on a server bound to 0.0.0.0 (line 211).",
