              "verdict": "FALSE_POSITIVE",
              "isFalsePositive": true,
              "reasoning": "The finding claims XXE at `ET.fromstring(xml)` (line 33). However, Python's standard `xml.etree.ElementTree` (which the function name `do_xml_etree_elementtree_findall` confirms is the parser in use) uses the expat parser, which does NOT resolve external entities. If an external entity reference is encountered, expat raises a `ParseError` rather than fetching the resource. Therefore, XXE is not possible through `ET.fromstring()` regardless of whether `xml` is attacker-controlled. The actual vulnerability in this function (if any) would be XPath injection via `user_input` in `findall()` on line 34, which is a different CWE and a different line than what is flagged.",
